use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Selection import Selection
from ../../../behaviors/Traversal import Traversal
from ../ToggleButton import ToggleButton

export ui-component ToggleGroup:
    description:
        A toggle group is a set of related ToggleButtons, like the Bold,
        Italic and Underline buttons in a text editor, or the alignment
        buttons next to them. It lets either one or any number of them be
        pressed at once.

    composes:
        - @{ToggleButton}

    behaviors:
        - @{Selection}
        - @{Traversal}

    modes:
        The component chooses whether one button or several can be pressed at
        a time. This is set once and doesn't change while it is in use.

    single:
        Pressing a button presses it in and pops out whichever was pressed
        before, as with text alignment. The component decides whether pressing
        the pressed button pops it out, leaving none pressed.

    multiple:
        Each button is pressed and popped out on its own, as with Bold and
        Italic. Pressing one leaves the others alone.

    keyboard:
        The group is one stop in the Tab order, landing on a pressed button,
        or the first available one if none is pressed. The arrow keys move
        focus between the buttons without pressing them, and Home and End go
        to the first and last. Pressing a button from the keyboard works the
        same as on any ToggleButton. By default the arrow keys wrap around at
        the ends, but the component can make them stop instead.

    layout:
        The buttons can be laid out in a row or a column. The arrow keys follow
        the direction they are laid out in.

    label:
        The group has a name for the whole set, such as "Text formatting", as
        well as each button having its own.

    disabled:
        The whole group can be disabled, as can individual buttons.

    nonGoals:
        - Pressed buttons are not saved with a form. A choice made in a form is
            a RadioGroup or a set of Checkboxes
        - Not for a choice where exactly one option must always be picked and
            moving to an option picks it. That's a SegmentedControl
